/* Card chrome for note embeds (`![[page]]`), so a transcluded statblock or moment section
   reads as a distinct card floating on the page rather than page content bleeding into the
   host note. Class names verified: .markdown-embed/.markdown-embed-title/.markdown-embed-content
   are Obsidian's own embed wrapper (used the same way multi-column.css and exemplar-layout.css
   already verify their own selectors). `.statblock-plugin-parent` is the Fantasy Statblocks
   plugin's real rendered-container class (grepped from the installed
   .obsidian/plugins/obsidian-5e-statblocks/styles.css, not guessed).

   A statblock embed (`![[<slug>-statblock]]`) already prints the creature's own name as its
   first line — Obsidian's default `.markdown-embed-title` bar above it duplicates that name, so
   it's suppressed only when the embed's content is a statblock; every other embed keeps its
   title bar. */
.markdown-embed {
  border: 1px solid var(--background-modifier-border);
  border-radius: 6px;
  background-color: var(--background-primary-alt);
  break-inside: avoid;
}

.markdown-embed:has(.statblock-plugin-parent) .markdown-embed-title {
  display: none;
}
